Ringer solution"},{"label":"D","text":"Apply pressure to the fundus with the palm of the hand and fingers in the direction of the long axis of the vagina"},{"label":"E","text":"Have the anesthesiologist adminis- ter halothane anesthesia for uterine relaxation Lactation, Puerperium, and Behavioral, Ethical, and Legal Problems 127"}],"priority":1,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Embryology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-10ac6615a59e","stem":"Following a vaginal delivery, a 265. A 31-year-old, gravida 3, para woman develops a fever, lower 3 Jehovah’s Witness begins to bleed abdominal pain, and uterine ten- heavily 2 days after a cesarean sec- derness. She is alert, and her blood tion. She refuses transfusion and pressure and urine output are good. says that she would rather die than Large gram-positive rods suggestive receive any blood or blood products. of clostridia are seen in a smear of You personally feel that you cannot the cervix. Which of the following watch her die and do nothing. is most closely tied to a decision to Appropriate actions that you can proceed with hysterectomy? take under these circumstances in","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Close observation for renal failure clude or hemolysis a. Telling the patient to find another"},{"label":"B","text":"Immediate radiographic examina- physician who will care for her tion for hydrosalpinx b. Transfusing her forcibly"},{"label":"C","text":"High-dose antibiotic therapy c. Letting her die, giving only sup-"},{"label":"D","text":"Fever of 103°C portive care"},{"label":"E","text":"Gas gangrene d. Getting a court order and transfus- ing"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-7bcc8c4a3fe8","stem":"Which of the following goes e. Having the patient’s husband sign a beyond what the federal Patient release to forcibly transfuse her Self-Determination Act requires hospitals to do for all patients ad- 266. Which of the following is mitted? beyond what a plaintiff must prove in a malpractice action in establish-a. Provide all adults with information ing the standard of care? about their right to accept or refuse treatment if life-threatening condi- a. A doctor-patient relationship was tions arise established","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Medical Ethics and Law","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"B","text":"State the institution’s policy on b. The defendant owed a duty to the advance directives patient"},{"label":"C","text":"Not discriminate in care given on c. The defendant breached a duty to the basis of patients’ wishes the patient"},{"label":"D","text":"Require assignment of donor organs d. The breach caused damage to the"},{"label":"E","text":"Allow patients to decide who has plaintiff the right to make decisions for them e. The duty is to give the best care possible in the given field 128 Obstetrics and Gynecology"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Medical Ethics and Law","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["possible_multiple_questions_in_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-1e2fbc28408a","stem":"A 27-year-old woman who 268. In which of the following sit- has previously received no prenatal uations should a court refuse to care presents at term. On ultrasound overturn a living will? she has a placenta previa, but she a. At the patient’s request, even if he refuses a cesarean section for any or she is delirious reason. Important points to consider b. If the patient is pregnant in her management include c. If it has been many years since the signinga. The obstetrician’s obligation to the","type":"Radiological Interpretation","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antenatal Care","options":[{"label":"D","text":"To allow an organ recipient 1 mo to supposedly normal fetus super- obtain a donated organ sedes the obligation to the healthy"},{"label":"E","text":"If there is testimony that the patient mother has changed his or her mind butb. The inclusion of several people did not revoke the will involved in this complex situation raises the legal risk to the physician"},{"label":"C","text":"Child abuse statutes require the physician to get a court order to force a cesarean section"},{"label":"D","text":"Court-ordered cesarean sections have almost always been deter- mined to achieve the best manage- ment"},{"label":"E","text":"A hospital ethics committee should be convened to evaluate the situa- tion LACTATION, PUERPERIUM, AND BEHAVIORAL, ETHICAL,AND LEGAL PROBLEMS Answers 238–239. The answers are 238-c, 239-b. (Cunningham, 20/e, pp 4, 538, 763, 1235.) A disadvantage of home delivery is the lack of facilities to con- trol postpartum hemorrhage. The woman described in the question deliv- ered a large baby, suffered multiple soft tissue injuries, and went into shock, needing 9 units of blood by the time she reached the hospital. Shee- han syndrome seems a likely possibility in this woman. This syndrome of anterior pituitary necrosis related to obstetric hemorrhage can be diag- nosed by 1 wk postpartum, as lactation fails to commence normally. Although many modern women choose hormonal therapy to prevent lac- tation, the woman described in the question was intent on breast feeding and so would not have received suppressant. She therefore could have been expected to begin lactation at the usual time. Other symptoms of Sheehan syndrome include amenorrhea, atrophy of the breasts, and loss of thyroid and adrenal function. The other presented choices for late sequelae are rather farfetched. Hemochromatosis would not be expected to occur in this healthy young woman, especially since she did not receive prolonged transfusions. Cushing, Simmonds, and Stein-Leventhal syndromes are not known to be related to postpartum hemorrhage. It is important to note that home delivery is not a predisposing factor to postpartum hemorrhage."}],"priority":1,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","duplicate_option_labels","requires_visual_review"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":true,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","long_option_manual_review","prior_structural_review_flag","requires_visual_review","topic_generic","visual_asset_not_transcribed"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"]},{"id":"q-faa72aec500b","stem":"The answer is e. (Ransom, 2000, pp 786–792.) Negligence law gov- erns conduct and embraces acts of both commission and omission, i.e., what a person did or failed to do. In general the law expects all persons to conduct themselves in a fashion that does not expose others to an unrea- sonable risk of harm. In a fiduciary relationship such as the physician- patient relationship, the physician is held to a higher standard of behavior because of the imbalance of knowledge. In general, the real gist of negli- gence is not carelessness or ineptitude, but rather how unreasonable the risk of harm the patient was exposed to by the physician’s action. Thus physicians are held accountable to a standard of care that asks the question, “What would the reasonable physician do under this specific set of cir- cumstances?","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-338fd5c0c32a","stem":"A 9-year-old girl presents forb. Liver disease with abnormal liver function tests evaluation of regular vaginal bleed","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"C","text":"Malignant melanoma ing. History reveals thelarche at age"},{"label":"D","text":"Undiagnosed genital tract bleeding 7 and adrenarche at age 8. The most"},{"label":"E","text":"Treated Stage III endometrial can- common cause of this condition in cer girls is"},{"label":"A","text":"Idiopathic"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topi