":"Cotrimoxazole (trimethoprim-sulfamethoxazole) for PCP prophylaxis should be initiated for which of the following patients?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"An adult with a CD4 count of 145"},{"label":"B","text":"A 2-year-old HIV-infected child with a CD4 count of 650 (21%)"},{"label":"C","text":"A 3 month old child whose HIV status is unknown, but who was born to an HIV positive mother"},{"label":"D","text":"All of the above (all need PCP prophylaxis)"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-24df86b610cc","stem":"An HIV-infected, two year old boy who is 10.5 kg is ready to be put on antiretroviral therapy for the first time. The child’s baseline hemoglobin is 10 g/dl. According to the national guidelines and drug indications, which regimen should you start the child on?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pharmacology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"AZT + 3TC + NVP"},{"label":"B","text":"AZT + 3TC + EFV"},{"label":"C","text":"D4T + 3TC + EFV"},{"label":"D","text":"D4T + ABC + LPV/r"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pharmacology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-6272f6700c54","stem":"Which of 