tic paralysis"},{"label":"D","text":"Justifies nursing the patient in an isolation ward"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e756481b387d","stem":"Iron deficiency anaemia","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Hematology","topic":"Hematology","topicOriginal":"Hematology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"May be prevented in infancy by early introduction of cows milk"},{"label":"B","text":"Is common finding in infant fed breast milk"},{"label":"C","text":"Predisposes children to recurrent infections"},{"label":"D","text":"Can be caused by infection of bone marrow"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Hematology","displayTopic":"Hematology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"7c3397409b7973f396836d86686d1143a8330b0b"},{"id":"q-044e43ac1c7b","stem":"A 1 week old term infant suddenly develops melena. The mother is healthy and the pregnancy was normal. The infant is breastfeeding. Hemoglobin is 77 g/L, Platelets are 599x 109/L. Differential white cell count is normal. Of the following the MOST likely cause of the bleeding is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Factor VIII deficiency ( Hemophilia)"},{"label":"B","text":"Factor IX deficiency"},{"label":"C","text":"Necrotizing enterocolitis"},{"label":"D","text":"Vitamin K deficiency"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-df7d626a697c","stem":"The amount of fluid deficit in a child with severe dehydration due to diarrhoea is approximately","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"250 ml /kg"},{"label":"B","text":"150ml/kg"},{"label":"C","text":"50ml/kg"},{"label":"D","text":"100ml/kg"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-51e3169a8662","stem":"Pyloric stenosis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"is due to thickening of the circular muscle fibres at the pylorus"},{"label":"B","text":"is inherited by the sex linked mode"},{"label":"C","text":"usually presents in the third month of life"},{"label":"D","text":"causes metabolic acidosis"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnsw