all pellets between index finger and thumb, sitting"},{"label":"B","text":"smiling, exchanging objects from hand to hand, rolling over, sitting unsupported"},{"label":"C","text":"laughing loud, exchanging objects from hand to hand, sitting and crawling"},{"label":"D","text":"smiling, holding objects when given but not reaching out for them, sitting unsupported, rolling over"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-212147cf41bf","stem":"Which of the following describes the position of the eyes in oculomotorius paresis of the left eye best?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Ophthalmology","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Both eyes are in the same axis when looking straight, left eye staying in midline when looking to the left"},{"label":"B","text":"Ptosis of left eyelid, downward and outward deviation of the left eye"},{"label":"C","text":"Left eye is constantly deviated to medial upward"},{"label":"D","text":"Left eye stays in midline when the right eye follows objects"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Ophthalmology","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-14b13e690752","stem":"The anterior fontanele usually feels closed on physical examination (palpation)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"between 3 and 9 months"},{"label":"B","text":"between 9 and 18 months"},{"label":"C","text":"between 18 and 24 months"},{"label":"D","text":"between 24 and 36 months"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"9fb6fcc6b4d3ab87d06332097a0855782761db2f"},{"id":"q-2273a69d2399","stem":"A cephalhematoma is best differentiated from caput succedaneum by","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"absence of a history of prolonged or difficult labor"},{"label":"B","text":"limitation of swelling to the area over one bone"},{"label":"C","text":"a normal neurologic examination"},{"label":"D","text":"a normal lumbar puncture"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-241a941e62b1","stem":"Which of the following is true about neonatal reflexes?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The ATNR (asymmetric tonic neck reflex) is abnormal at all ages"},{"label":"B","text":"The Moro reflex is only abnormal when it is absent in a child below 6 months."},{"label":"C","text":"The plantar (foot) grasp reflex should be lost by the time the child can pull himself up to stand and walk along objects"},{"label":"D","text":"If walking is practiced while the walking reflex is present, the baby learns faster how to walk."}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-539b97a67f85","stem":"The APGAR Score","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"assesses heart- rate, respiration, colour, reaction to stimulus and muscle tone directly after birth repeatedly over at least 10 minutes"},{"label":"B","text":"should be done at 5, 10, 20 and 30 minutes in every baby"},{"label":"C","text":"always predicts a poor neurological outcome if it is below 6"},{"label":"D","text":"should only be done in babies who fail to suck after delivery"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-61ab208d29f4","stem":"Which of the following blood group constellation is common in ABO incompatibility and why?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Mother group A, Baby group O, because mother’ s red blood cells are hemolysed in the babies body by the babies antibodies"},{"label":"B","text":"Mother Group A, Baby group B, because mother develops IG M antibodies against B, and these cross the placenta"},{"label":"C","text":"Mother group O, Baby group A or B, because mother develops IGM antibodies against A and B, and these cross the placenta"},{"label":"D","text":"Mother group O, Baby group A or B, as mother develops IG G antibodies against A or B, and these cross the placenta"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2cdd5cdd16d9","stem":"Which of the following CSF ( cerebrospinal fluid) results would be the most typical for TB-Meningitis?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Protein 2.2 g/dl, Glucose 0.1mmol/l, 600 WBC, 97% Polymorphs"},{"label":"B","text":"Protein 1.8 g/dl, Glucose 0.1mmol/l, 90 WBC, 92% Lymphocytes"},{"label":"C","text":"Protein 0.4 g/dl, Glucose 1.5 mmol/l, 12 WBC, 92% Lymphocytes"},{"label":"D","text":"Protein 1.0 g/dl, Glucose 3 mmol/l, 56 WBC, 95% Lymphocytes"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOp