HO classification?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"CXR showing bilateral infiltrates"},{"label":"B","text":"Tachypnea, subcostal indrawings, ill looking"},{"label":"C","text":"Tachypnea, Leucocytosis in Full Blood picture"},{"label":"D","text":"Cyanosis and clubbing"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-3f818908403b","stem":"How long after exposure to Measles can you protect a susceptible Measles-contact from getting the disease by giving live-vaccination?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"not at all"},{"label":"B","text":"24 hours"},{"label":"C","text":"72 hours"},{"label":"D","text":"5 days"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-11dd80f8e6f7","stem":"If you were asked to set up a national policy on Rubella vaccination in a country with limited resources, which group of people would you vaccinate?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"labe